          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"NET0011\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"/NET0004\") ... (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"4\")) (node (ref \"R1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"Net-(Q1-B)\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"B\")) (node (ref \"R9\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"14\") (name \"Net-(Q1-C)\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\")) (node (ref \"Q3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The fan PWM command also switches its supply, so the fan cannot receive an independent PWM speed-control signal and may lose power during PWM operation.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U2.1", "U3.1", "U2.2", "U3.2", "U2.3", "U3.3", "U2.4", "U3.4", "U2.5", "U3.5", "U2.6", "U3.6", "U2.7", "U3.7", "U2.8", "U3.8"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND", "NET0002", "NET0003", "NET0006", "NET0010", "NET0011", "NET0012"],
      "observed": "The ATtiny13 (U2) and ATtiny45 (U3) are both present in the netlist, and their corresponding supply, ground, reset, and GPIO pins are connected to the same nets.",
      "expected": "Two independently populated microcontrollers should not have their GPIO outputs tied together. If these are alternate MCU choices, the design or assembly configuration should ensure only one is populated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"7\") (name \"NET0003\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"NET0011\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"5\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are populated and firmware configures shared pins as outputs, they can contend electrically; even without contention, the two devices cannot operate as independent controllers. The netlist alone does not establish whether one is intended to be left unpopulated.",
      "confidence": 0.74
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The same MCU signal drives both the fan's pin-4 control line and the transistor that switches fan power, coupling PWM operation to supply switching. The netlist also places two microcontrollers on shared GPIO nets, which is hazardous if both are populated."
}

